<title>USA: Natl Datacomputer sets reverse split.</title>
<headline>Natl Datacomputer sets reverse split.</headline>
<dateline>BILLERICA, Mass. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>National DataComputer Inc said Thursday it had declared a one-for-four reverse stock split.</p>
<p>The shares begin trading at post-split prices today, it said.</p>
<p>The company had about 4.9 million shares outstanding prior to the split. After the split, it has about 1.2 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The company said the purpose of the split was to push up its stock price. The stock needs to trade above $3 a share for it to be relisted on the Nasdaq SmallCap Market.</p>
</text>
